-    if (op.name === 'query') {
-      const { awaitPendingSearchCacheWrites } = await import('./core/search/hybrid.ts');
-      await awaitPendingSearchCacheWrites();
+    // Drain fire-and-forget PGLite writes (cache.store, bumpLastRetrievedAt,
+    // bumpHit) before the finally-disconnect closes _db. Covers query AND
+    // search — both fire bumpLastRetrievedAt + share the same race surface.
+    if (op.name === 'query' || op.name === 'search' || op.name === 'get_page') {
+      const { awaitPendingWrites } = await import('./core/pending-writes.ts');
+      await awaitPendingWrites();
     }
```

## Verification

Same 500-record PGLite brain that reproduced the hang.

| | Before patch | After patch |
|---|---|---|
| `gbrain query "Wer ist Nevena Savic?" --no-expand --limit 5` | exit 142 after 90s | exit 0 in 1.1s |
| `gbrain query "..." --limit 5` (with google:gemini-2.5-flash-lite expansion) | exit 142 after 90s | exit 0 in 2.5s |
| `gbrain search "Nevena Savic" --limit 3` | exit 0 in 0.8s (was a partial race — search wins because UPDATE is faster than disconnect) | exit 0 in 0.8s (now deterministic — drain awaits the UPDATE) |

## Aside

While diagnosing I also noticed: `recordSpend` (`operations.ts:3761`, image-search path) and `telemetry.flush` (`telemetry.ts:103`) use the same untracked `void ...` pattern, but neither blocked exit in my testing — `recordSpend` only fires for image search, and `telemetry.flush` already explicitly drops on CLI exit per the comment at `telemetry.ts:189`. Left them alone; happy to wrap them too if you want defense-in-depth.

