- The batch `flush()` in these paths swallows write errors entirely in `--json` mode (`if (!jsonMode) console.error(...)`) — didn't matter here (nothing threw; the JOIN just matched nothing), but it makes this class of bug even harder to see. A one-line stderr emit regardless of json mode might be worth it.
